.\" groff -man -Tascii setgid.2
.\"
.TH SETGID 2 "January 2026" "TestUnix Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
setgid \- set group identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/types.h>
.br
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int setgid(gid_t " gid ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B setgid()
sets the effective group ID of the calling process. If the calling process is privileged, the real GID and saved set-group-ID are also set.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned. On error, -1 is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EPERM
The user is not privileged and
.I gid
does not match the real GID or saved set-group-ID of the calling process.
